Track 1: Freeze-Tag the Horizon
- Story & Context: Outside the abandoned port warehouse in San Pedro where the 2003 totality began, teenager Mateo rigged a car horn to a swingbeat drum machine, sparking a confrontation with city guards as the moon crossed the sun. The sound caught fire across local pirate radio, turning a street game into a synchronized riot chant: "You stop moving when the sky goes black, you don't turn around till we give it back!" The resulting track layered that chanted threat over a grinding sub-bass drone and overdriven Korg brass stabs. It marked the precise moment the carnival sound system culture mutated into something angry, industrial, and fast.
