Track 3: Red Light, Black Sun
- Story & Context: Legend says Reducto recorded the final master of this track during a three-minute eclipse over an illegal highway block party in 2007, using a mobile rig powered by six car batteries. As the darkness reached its peak, a police blockade surrounded the crowd, but the massive low-end drone vibrated the asphalt so violently it tripped the precinct's local power grid. The crowd dispersed into the dark leaving only the looping CD playing through a burning speaker tower, whispering the haunting final refrain: "Run all the lights you want, the sky is already red." It remains the undisputed blueprint of the Eclipse-Jack movement, played at every eclipse gathering since.
